  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The person in the wheelchair is mapped as 'not any different' from others",
  "description": "The text 'i'm not any different' is overlaid on the image of a person in a wheelchair, creating an analogical mapping where the person in the wheelchair is being equated with 'any different' — implying they are not fundamentally different from non-disabled people. This mapping is central to the meme's intent to challenge ableist assumptions, though it may inadvertently reinforce 'inspiration porn' tropes by framing the person's disability as something to be overcome or celebrated rather than accepted as part of their identity. The visual entity (person_in_wheelchair) is mapped onto the textual concept of 'not any different' — asserting their equality and normalcy despite their physical disability.",
